3. 養聲

廣東話：佢係歌手，日日都要飲啖湯養聲。
English: He's a singer, so he has to drink soup every day to take care of his voice.

4. 票尾

廣東話：記得收好張票尾，遲啲要攞嚟對獎㗎。
English: Remember to keep the ticket stub, you'll need it to check the lottery results later.

5. hacker

廣東話：嗰個 hacker 好勁，一晚就 hack 埋成間公司嘅系統。
English: That hacker is really skilled, he hacked the whole company's system in one night.

6. 石斛蘭

廣東話：阿婆最鍾意喺露台種石斛蘭，話啲花好靚。
English: Grandma loves growing dendrobium orchids on the balcony, she says the flowers are beautiful.

7. 吊詭

廣東話：呢個問題好吊詭，越諗越覺得矛盾。
English: This question is quite paradoxical, the more you think about it, the more contradictory it seems.

8. 吊詭

廣東話：佢講嘅嘢聽落好荒謬，但細心諗吓又似非而是，真係好吊詭。
English: What he said sounds absurd, but if you think about it carefully, it seems paradoxically true.

9. 各為其主

廣東話：我哋雖然係朋友，但喺談判桌上各為其主，冇辦法。
English: Although we're friends, on the negotiation table we each serve our own boss, there's no way around it.

10. 軨蓋

廣東話：架車嘅軨蓋花咗，要攞去整先得。
English: The wheel cover of the car is scratched, it needs to be repaired.

11. 打哥夫

廣東話：禮拜六有冇興趣一齊去打哥夫？
English: Are you interested in playing golf together on Saturday?

12. 免揀

廣東話：呢間舖頭啲衫全部免揀，唔鍾意就唔好買。
English: All the clothes in this shop are non-selectable, if you don't like them, don't buy them.

13. 擺闊佬

廣東話：佢份人工唔高，但成日請人食飯擺闊佬。
English: His salary isn't high, but he always treats people to meals to show off his wealth.

14. 廣播劇

廣東話：以前啲人放學返屋企就會扭開收音機聽廣播劇。
English: In the past, people would turn on the radio to listen to radio dramas after school.

15. 錄影機

廣東話：而家好少人仲用錄影機㗎喇，個個都上網睇片。
English: Hardly anyone uses video recorders nowadays, everyone watches videos online.

16. 吟詩吟唔甩

廣東話：閉路電視影到晒佢偷嘢嘅過程，今次佢吟詩吟唔甩喇。
English: The CCTV captured the whole process of him stealing, this time he can't deny it at all.

17. 佈道大會

廣東話：教會下個禮拜會喺體育館舉行一場佈道大會。
English: The church will hold an evangelistic rally at the stadium next week.

18. 寫手

廣東話：佢係雜誌社嘅寫手，日日都要交稿。
English: He's a writer at the magazine, he has to submit articles every day.

19. 寫手

廣東話：聽講有啲學生搵寫手幫手寫論文，真係唔應該。
English: I heard some students hire ghostwriters to write their essays, that's really not right.

20. 代打

廣東話：我打唔贏呢個 boss，不如搵人代打啦。
English: I can't beat this boss, maybe I should find someone to play on my behalf.

21. 茶碗

廣東話：呢隻茶碗係日本帶返嚟嘅，好靚。
English: This tea bowl was brought back from Japan, it's very beautiful.

22. 茶隔

廣東話：沖茶之前記得擺個茶隔喺杯上面，唔係啲茶葉會飲入口。
English: Remember to put the tea strainer on the cup before pouring tea, otherwise you'll drink the tea leaves.

23. 只許州官放火，不准百姓點燈

廣東話：老細可以遲到，我哋遲到就扣人工，真係只許州官放火，不准百姓點燈。
English: The boss can be late but we get our pay docked if we're late, it's really a case of "one rule for the rich and another for the poor".

24. 獨唱

廣東話：音樂會嗰晚，佢會獨唱一首英文歌。
English: At the concert that night, she will sing an English song solo.

25. 快人快事

廣東話：佢一聽完就即刻答應幫手，真係快人快事！
English: He agreed to help right after hearing about it, what a straightforward and satisfying thing to do!

26. 四腳獸

廣東話：聽講嗰個公廁成日有人做四腳獸，搞到好污糟。
English: I heard people often engage in "four-legged beast" activities in that public toilet, making it very dirty.

27. 無米粥

廣東話：呢單嘢而家仲係煲緊無米粥，等傾掂咗先話你知。
English: This matter is still at the preliminary discussion stage, I'll let you know once it's settled.

28. 義會

廣東話：以前啲街坊冇錢周轉，就會夾錢做義會。
English: In the old days, neighbours who needed money would pool their money together in a rotating credit association.

29. 榜文

廣東話：博物館入面展覽咗一張清朝嘅榜文。
English: A Qing dynasty official notice is on display in the museum.

30. MK名

廣東話：佢個網名叫做「★唯愛℡仔仔★」，好明顯係 MK 名啦。
English: His online name is "★唯愛℡仔仔★", it's obviously a typical "MK" style name. [end of text]


